WEBVTT

00:03:59.610 --> 00:04:03.698
In 1258 CE, the Mongols
approached Baghdad.

00:04:03.990 --> 00:04:07.618
They encountered little resistance 
as they thoroughly destroyed the city.

00:04:07.952 --> 00:04:10.705
Legend has it that they rolled
the caliph in a rug

00:04:10.705 --> 00:04:12.748
and had horses trample him to death,

00:04:12.999 --> 00:04:16.210
and that the Tigris River ran
black from the ink of the manuscripts

00:04:16.210 --> 00:04:17.837
that were thrown into it.

00:04:18.587 --> 00:04:22.049
The siege of Baghdad laid bare
a longstanding reality:

00:04:22.300 --> 00:04:26.053
for centuries, the caliphs had
ruled mostly symbolically.

00:04:26.512 --> 00:04:29.724
Local leaders throughout the empire
had grown more powerful,

00:04:29.724 --> 00:04:31.726
and they refused to pay taxes,